const t=["Record","Notify and allow response","Collect evidence","Classify","Decide proportionate action","Document outcome"],a=["A missed deadline or a genuine crop failure is never labelled fraud.","No one is labelled publicly. Case details are visible to the people involved and to administrators only.","No automatic seizure or penalty. Any recovery follows the signed agreement and a recorded decision.","The affected party is told, can respond and can dispute the case at any time.","Confirmed fraud or breach needs a second reviewer who is a different administrator."],r={"Missed reporting deadline":{blurb:"A late report is an administrative matter first. It says nothing about honesty.",guard:"A missed deadline is not a finding of fault and is never treated as fraud.",steps:["The date the report was due and the date this was flagged are on record.","Remind the cooperative of the missing report and give a fair window to respond or explain.","Collect the late report, the cooperative explanation and any proof of the cause (for example flooding, illness or no network).","Decide whether this was reasonable cause, an administrative lapse or a repeated lapse.","Choose the lightest action that fixes the problem: a reminder, a new deadline or a follow up call.","Write down what was decided and why, then close the case."],classifications:["Reasonable cause explained","Administrative lapse, report now received","Repeated lapse, support plan needed"],actions:["Send a reminder only","Agree a new reporting date","Arrange a support call with the cooperative","Escalate for review if reports keep being missed"]},"Project delay":{blurb:"Delays are common in farming. The aim is a realistic new plan, not blame.",guard:"A delay is not a finding of fault. Weather, supply and logistics are weighed first.",steps:["The delayed activity, the original date and the expected new date are on record.","Ask the cooperative what caused the delay and give them time to reply.","Collect supplier notes, delivery records, weather information or inspection reports.","Decide the cause: weather, supply, capacity, or something that needs a closer look.","Choose the response: a revised timeline, moving a tranche date, or practical support.","Record the agreed plan and close the case once the activity is back on track."],classifications:["Weather or season related","Supplier or logistics delay","Cooperative capacity gap","Cause not yet clear"],actions:["Approve a revised timeline","Move the next tranche date","Arrange extra supervision or support","Keep monitoring with a check date"]},"Disputed expense":{blurb:"An expense that does not match a quotation needs an explanation before any conclusion.",guard:"A price difference or missing paperwork is not misuse. The cooperative can explain and dispute.",steps:["The expense, the approved quotation and the invoice amount are on record.","Ask the cooperative and the supplier to explain the difference.","Collect the invoice, quotation, delivery note and payment proof.","Decide whether this is a documentation gap, a justified price change or an ineligible expense.","Choose the action: accept with a note, correct the record, or ask for the excess to be returned.","Record the decision. Any correction is a new entry. The original record stays."],classifications:["Documentation gap, resolved","Justified price variance","Expense not eligible under the budget"],actions:["Accept the expense with a note","Post a correcting entry","Ask for the excess amount to be returned through the agreed process","Request a revised budget approval"]},"Genuine crop failure":{blurb:"Crop failure is a risk the agreement shares. It is assessed on evidence and never treated as fraud.",guard:"A genuine crop failure is not fraud and does not by itself trigger any penalty.",steps:["The report of loss, the date and the affected plots are on record.","Confirm receipt to the cooperative and tell them what evidence will help.","Collect photos, GPS, community statements and an independent assessor report. These support but do not prove the loss.","Decide whether the loss is genuine, partly preventable, or not yet established.","Follow the signed agreement: insurance claim, rescheduling or restructuring, or a loss sharing arrangement.","Record the outcome and how remaining obligations will be handled, then close the case."],classifications:["Genuine crop failure (not fraud)","Partly preventable, support plan agreed","Not yet established, more evidence needed"],actions:["Start an insurance claim where cover exists","Reschedule the repayment","Restructure the repayment terms","Apply the loss sharing clause of the agreement"]},"Inability to repay":{blurb:"Struggling to repay is handled through the agreement. It is not a presumption of bad faith.",guard:"Inability to repay is not fraud. No automatic seizure. Recovery follows the agreement only.",steps:["The amount due, the date and what has been paid are on record.","Tell the cooperative and the investors involved, and invite a repayment proposal.","Collect sales records, buyer balances and the cooperative proposal.","Decide whether the cash problem is temporary or structural.","Choose from rescheduling, restructuring, a payment plan or the recovery steps in the agreement.","Record the agreed plan and who will track it, then close the case."],classifications:["Temporary cash flow gap","Waiting on buyer payment","Structural shortfall, restructuring needed"],actions:["Reschedule the repayment date","Agree a part payment plan","Restructure the terms with all parties","Begin the agreed recovery process (no automatic seizure)"]},"Suspected misuse of funds":{blurb:"A report of misuse is a concern to investigate, not a conclusion.",guard:"Suspicion is not proof. Do not label anyone. Pausing new payments is a precaution, not a penalty.",steps:["The report, who made it and the funds involved are on record. Evidence is preserved.","Tell the cooperative what is being reviewed and give them a fair chance to explain.","Collect receipts, delivery records, bank confirmations and independent statements.","Decide whether the concern is unsubstantiated, a policy breach, or needs escalation.","Consider pausing new disbursements where the agreement allows, an independent review, or recovery steps.","Record the decision and the reasons, tell the parties, then close the case."],classifications:["Unsubstantiated after review","Misapplication of funds, a breach of the budget","Serious concern, escalate for second review"],actions:["Keep new disbursements paused where the agreement permits","Commission an independent review","Agree a repayment of misapplied amounts","Escalate to the second reviewer"]},"Confirmed fraud or breach":{blurb:"The most serious category. It needs strong evidence, a second reviewer and a right to respond.",guard:"Needs a second reviewer who is a different administrator. No public labelling and no automatic seizure.",needsSecondReviewer:!0,steps:["The finding that led to this case and the funds involved are on record. Evidence is preserved.","Give the affected party written notice and a full chance to respond and dispute.","Collect the evidence file: documents, statements, confirmations and the response received.","Decide whether the evidence supports a confirmed breach. A second reviewer must also agree.","Choose a proportionate action under the agreement: termination, recovery through the agreed process, or referral to the proper authority.","Record the signed off decision, who was told and what happens next, then close the case."],classifications:["Breach of agreement confirmed","Fraud confirmed on evidence","Not confirmed, case downgraded for review"],actions:["Terminate further funding under the agreement","Start recovery through the agreed legal process","Refer to the proper authority where the law requires","Downgrade to a lower category for review"]}},o=["High","Medium","Low"],n=["Open","Under Review","Awaiting Response","Escalated","Resolved"];function i(e){return e.status==="Resolved"?6:e.status==="Escalated"?3:e.status==="Awaiting Response"||e.status==="Under Review"?2:1}export{n as C,a as G,t as P,r as R,o as S,i as d};
